Q: C thread deadlock debug regarding a thread synchronization assignment A: <p>Why are you using <strong>three</strong> semaphores in the first place? You only need <strong>one</strong> semaphore.</p>
<p>Have <code>main()</code> initialize that single semaphore with a value of 6 (not 5!), start <em>all 40</em> threads at once, and then wait for all 40 threads to end.</p>
<p>The first thing each thread needs to do is lock the semaphore. The 1st 6 threads will succeed, the other 34 threads will wait.</p>
<p>Each thread needs to unlock the semaphore 1 time before exiting, except for thread 10 which needs to unlock the semaphore 6 times before exiting.</p>
<p>Each time the semaphore is unlocked, a waiting thread will stop waiting. Eventually, all 40 threads will have a chance to run.</p>
<p>That's it. Don't over-complicate things.</p>
<p>Try this:</p>
<pre class="lang-c prettyprint-override"><code>#include &lt;pthread.h&gt;
#include &lt;semaphore.h&gt;
#include &lt;unistd.h&gt;
#include &lt;stdio.h&gt;
// ...

typedef struct thread_arg {
    pid_t process_n
    int thread_n;
    pthread_t thread_id;
    sem_t *sem;
    // ...
} thread_arg_t;

enum message_type {
    BEGIN,
    END
};

void info(enum message_type msg, pid_t process_n, int thread_n) {
    // ...
}

void* thread_proc(void* arg){
    thread_arg_t *thread_info = (thread_arg_t*)arg;

    info(BEGIN, thread_info-&gt;process_n, thread_info-&gt;thread_n);

    sem_wait(thread_info-&gt;sem);

    // ...

    if (thread_info-&gt;thread_n == 10) {
        for (int i = 0; i &lt; 5; ++i) {
            sem_post(thread_info-&gt;sem);
        }
    }

    sem_post(thread_info-&gt;sem);

    info(END, thread_info-&gt;process_n, thread_info-&gt;thread_n);
    return NULL;
}

int main() {
    thread_arg_t threads[40];
    sem_t sem;

    pid_t pid = getpid();

    if (sem_init(&amp;sem, 0, 6) &lt; 0){
        perror(&quot;Error initializing the semaphore!&quot;);
        return 2;
    }

    for (int i = 0; i &lt; 40; ++i) {
        threads[i].process_n = pid;
        threads[i].thread_n = i+1;
        threads[i].sem = &amp;sem;
        // ...

        if (pthread_create(&amp;threads[i].thread_id, NULL, &amp;thread_proc, &amp;threads[i]) != 0) {
            perror(&quot;Error initializing a thread!&quot;);
            return 2;
        }
    }

    for (int i = 0; i &lt; 40; ++i) {
        pthread_join(threads[i].thread_id, NULL);
    }

    sem_destroy(&amp;sem);

    return 0;
}
</code></pre>
